A||||7||isthiswhereiputausername?||car acting funny on long drive (2 questions)||||9||
Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-16-2001||08:26 AM||||Drove my car to work today.. longest drive it had in 3 years (30 miles - highway) but about 5 miles away from my work it started missing and backfiring a few times, then my tach was jumping slightly the rest of the way, (sounded like my valves ticking a little louder too)..  then when I did get to work, I shut it off and retried to start it again.. it turned over really slow (like a dead battery)and wouldnt start.. then i let it sit for about 30 seconds and it started up but really slow on the starter.. <P>would it be a bad coil that got corroded when it was sitting 3 years?<P>The engine is a 85 2.8 L carbed motor.<BR>(new gas and new plugs/oil)<P><BR>And on another note.... Do GM alternators die with no reason?  I had my wifes car laid up this weekend(replacing struts) and when I started it back up, the battery light wouldnt go out.. take the battery cable off..stalls(indicates a bad alt right?) and when I ran the alt test as outlined in my mitchell repair cd, it showed that the alt was dead..<BR>We never had any problems with it before.. (tempest..2.8 MPFI)<P>Thanks<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Raydar||10-16-2001||10:08 AM||||<BR>GM alternators can up and die with no notice whatsoever. Try unclipping/reclipping the black two-wire plug from the alternator. Sometimes the connections get dirty. Many times the regulator/rectifier(?) board will become intermittant. Heat and vibration take their toll on the solder joints. <P>As for the Fiero...  I was going to say it was the coil, tach filter or ignition module, until I read that it turned over slowly when you cranked it. Almost sounds like the battery is run down. Either that or you have an ignition problem *and* a bad starter. Or loose connections. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula||10-16-2001||10:36 AM||||my starter did that too.  I ended up replacing the motor (for different reasons).<P>But it seemed like it was the starter or alternator||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-16-2001||10:36 AM||||just went out and tried it now..started up first turn and sounds great again..<P>It must be the coil getting hot  on the long drives correct?<P>Think I will replace my starter also since I have a spare one on my parts car.<P>As far as the tempest alt,all the wires do look good and when I unplugged it, the dash light went out and when I grounded the "L" wire the dash light went back on. (GM's alt test)<BR>The  car worked great before I switched struts then when I started it afterwards..the light was on..(dont think I hit any wires..everything looks ok)<P>thanks for the replys guys!<p>[This message has been edited by isthiswhereiputausername? (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
